{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== HANDOFF #17 — SESSION END. e369 + parity epic 3e73. READ THIS, THEN #16, THEN #15. ===\n\nWORKTREE /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-jira-family (currently on branch worktree-main tracking origin/main).\nALWAYS: export PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\". DO NOT trust the board below — read the tickets.\nA spare worktree /Users/joeoakhart/agent-5200-diag is kept parked on gerrit/main FOR CLOSES.\n\n*** WHERE THIS STANDS ***\ne369: **31/35 closed.** OPEN: 5200, 751e, 2b16 (all in_progress), 88d9 (open).\n3e73: **4/6 closed.** ALL FOUR P1 CHILDREN CLOSED (cedc, 79d5, 2944, bd9e) — half the stop condition\n  is permanently met. OPEN: 0fad (close was running at session end — RE-CHECK IT FIRST), 2127 (leave).\nThe DC feature's headline behaviour is PROVEN LIVE in both directions and has stayed proven across\nfive harness runs. What remains is a tail of DC write-path defects the new parity tests exposed.\n\n*** THE OPERATOR'S SCOPE RULING — the single most important thing to carry ***\nJ11's seven new mutation cells found THREE more DC defects. Asked whether they gate e369, the operator\nchose the STRICTEST option: **ALL THREE ARE e369 CHILDREN AND MUST BE FIXED BEFORE THE EPIC CLOSES.**\nThey are reparented. Do not quietly demote them to follow-ups.\n\n--- IMMEDIATE NEXT ACTIONS, in order ---\n 1. **Re-check 0fad's close.** A close was in flight at session end (it first failed for a missing\n    `--class`; retried with `--class preexisting`). Its change 1255 is MERGED. If it did not land,\n    just re-run the close from the spare worktree.\n 2. **Two fix agents were RUNNING and may have finished or died — CHECK GERRIT AND THE TICKETS, do not\n    assume.** 049e (DC comment ceiling configurable) and 751e (DC clear-assignee never unassigns).\n    Neither had pushed a change at session end. If an agent died, its ticket comments record how far it\n    got; re-dispatch from there rather than restarting.\n 3. **2b16 is CERTIFIED AND CLAIMED, ready to implement.** Then 88d9. **SERIALIZE THEM — both modify\n    `inbound_differ.py`.** 88d9 is unsigned but its file impact is declared, so its review can run.\n 4. **a3fa** is unsigned, file impact declared, NOT an e369 child and does not gate the epic.\n 5. **Re-run the harness** once 751e/2b16/88d9 land. Three of J11's new cells are EXPECTED RED until\n    then (`test_outbound_unassign_round_trips`, `test_inbound_delete_link_round_trips`,\n    `test_inbound_clear_parent_round_trips`). **DO NOT INVERT THEM TO MAKE CI GREEN** — they assert the\n    correct contract and their redness is the point.\n 6. **Then close 5200, then e369.** e369's own plan review is `stale-code` and must be re-run before its\n    close will pass.\n\n--- THE GENERALISATION THIS EPIC EARNED. Carry this above any individual ticket. ---\n**\"CLOUD HAS THE TRANSLATION, DC NEVER GOT ITS HALF\" — now FOUR instances, all silent:**\n  * d067 — outbound status submitted as a REST field edit, never a transition. Cloud routes it in\n    `acli.py:170,182-183`. Soft-failed, exit 0, status silently unchanged.\n  * 8d68 — inbound UPDATE handed the mint a bare string; it returns at `isinstance(assignee, dict)`.\n    The CREATE path passes a dict and works, which is why it stayed invisible.\n  * 751e — empty assignee reaches `assign_issue` as `\"\"`; pycontribs treats only None/-1/\"-1\" as\n    Unassigned. Cloud has the fix at `acli.py:342-345,357-359` (bug 85a1).\n  * 2b16 / 88d9 — the inbound-mirroring variant: link removal and parent clear are never emitted at\n    all, while outbound has the removal path.\nEVERY ONE was a silent success — no traceback, no alert, pass reports OK. When touching any Cloud/DC\nshared seam, CHECK BOTH SIDES BEFORE ASSUMING PARITY, and never accept \"no exception raised\" as\nevidence a write landed.\n\n--- WHY THE PARITY WORK WAS THE RIGHT INVESTMENT (the evidence, for anyone who doubts it) ---\n * 2944's ledger ran the 429 mutation under the ORIGINAL assertions and it **passed green** — a direct\n   demonstration that the old test could not fail, not an argument that it couldn't.\n * cedc's `WIKI_DESCRIPTION_LIMIT 32767 -> 32766` mutation initially SURVIVED, because its at-limit\n   pins derived their boundary from the IMPORTED constant. 79d5's agent hit the identical defect class\n   independently, in different files. Both fixed by pinning module-local literals. **Never pin a\n   boundary against the constant under test.**\n * 79d5: dropping the DC sanitizer injection left CONVERGENCE passing, because DC's and Cloud's comment\n   truncation output is byte-identical (same 32767, same suffix). Only a RECORDING check caught it.\n * 8d68 exists at all because J11's assignee oracle was vacuous. Repaired, it immediately found a real\n   defect that had been reported green for months.\n * 0fad corrected an assumption rather than confirming one: Cloud's whole-project readers page by\n   OPAQUE CURSOR, not offset arithmetic, so the DC truncation family structurally cannot occur there\n   (measured: 250 recovered even with pages capped at 40 while 100 was requested). Its deliverable\n   became a regression net — which then caught a DIFFERENT real defect,\n   [rebar:cabc-7a98-d173-4d7c]: those readers SPIN FOREVER on a repeated cursor token, a guard\n   `fetcher._iter_pages` already has at `fetcher.py:286-308`. Committed as `xfail(strict=True)`.\n\n--- FOLLOW-UPS FILED, NONE GATING e369 ---\n  cabc (Cloud readers spin on repeated cursor) · a3fa (capability sites cast but not runtime-guarded)\n  d582 (rekey live cell derives a colliding project key ~1 run in 26) · 9fb3 (no CI coverage of the\n  inspect-ai [eval] path, and `[tool.uv] conflicts` makes it structurally uncoverable by the normal\n  suite) · 63e8 (a committed lock turns any future transitive-dep advisory into a build stoppage —\n  wants a runbook) · 3b5f (dead `(inbound, probe)` dispatch chain; 0 ACs, needs shaping).\n\n--- 2127: DO NOT START IT ---\nDiverged over EIGHT review rounds, every finding reviewer-correct. Cloud has FIVE distinct 429\nbehaviours, not the two its plan assumed, plus a name collision between two `update_priority`\nimplementations. It needs someone to settle Cloud's retry taxonomy first. P2, Cloud-side, droppable.\n\n--- TRAPS ADDED THIS SESSION (earlier ones in #16/#15/#14/#13 still hold and are still true) ---\n * **SHELL BACKTICKS IN A `rebar comment` ARGUMENT ARE COMMAND-SUBSTITUTED AND SILENTLY DELETE TEXT.**\n   Cost three load-bearing sentences on 8d68 — and the comment still landed at a plausible length, so\n   neither the exit code nor a byte check caught it. Use a quoted heredoc into a file, pass\n   `\"$(cat f)\"`, then GREP THE STORED COMMENT for identifiers you expect.\n * **VERIFY A WRITE WITH A PREDICATE THAT MATCHES WHAT YOU WROTE.** I checked a bd9e comment for a\n   harness run id it never contained, concluded failure, and re-posted four times.\n * **`--ref` DOES NOT SATISFY THE file_impact CLOSE PRECHECK.** A ticket with declared file_impact needs\n   a referencing commit reachable from the WORKTREE's HEAD. Keep a worktree parked on gerrit/main.\n * **CHECK gerrit/main, NOT origin/main, AFTER A SUBMIT.** The mirror lags and made merged work look\n   absent.\n * **A `Verified -1` CAN COME FROM A RUN THAT TESTED NOTHING.** `gerrit-verify.yaml`'s concurrency group\n   does not isolate per change under load; dispatches seconds apart cancel each other and the\n   `if: always()` vote job still votes -1 with `build-and-test` SKIPPED. Check the JOB LIST. Recheck ONE\n   change at a time. Rebase-If-Necessary applies at SUBMIT, not to CI — a change pushed before a fix\n   landed needs a REBASE, not a recheck.\n * **`docs/env-vars.md` RECORDS LINE NUMBERS**, so a pure import insertion above an env read fails the\n   drift gate. Run `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py`, in the change that shifts the line.\n * **The 800-LOC cap applies ONLY to `src/**`** (both enforcers rglob `src_root`). Do not split a\n   live-suite test module to satisfy it — that risks dropping it from the `_live_jira_ready` canary.\n * **`relation_snapshot.py:141` aborts on ANY non-empty `git status --porcelain` in the shared tracker**,\n   untracked files included. That, not lock contention, causes `store-read-failure`/INDETERMINATE.\n * **`constraint-dependencies` cannot lift an upstream cap — it only narrows.** Its confident\n   UNSATISFIABLE is an artifact of the instrument, and I nearly suppressed a real CVE on the strength\n   of it. `override-dependencies` REPLACES the requirement. (Fix landed via ticket 1dfd; reasoning is\n   preserved on 1dfd and on e47e.)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785725278038521001,"uuid":"17801fe1-0dbf-423b-bffa-395314f0cc3f"}